Lipi Terminal

Lipi Terminal is an independent experimental fork of iTerm2.
It is not an official iTerm2 release.

iTerm2 was created by George Nachman and its contributors.
Upstream project: https://github.com/gnachman/iTerm2
Upstream documentation: https://iterm2.com

The existing LICENSE and COPYING files are retained without modification.
LICENSE contains GNU General Public License version 2. COPYING states GPL
version 2 or later and notes that Apache 2.0-licensed dependencies make the
combined distribution effectively GPL version 3. Third-party components retain
their respective licenses and notices; this notice does not replace them.

Fork changes add experimental opt-in Malayalam and Hindi natural-text layout,
terminal-cell projection, selection/copy and wrapping behavior, responsive table
layout, and Hindi font selection. The fork's name and packaging distinguish it
from upstream; no upstream endorsement is implied.

The Lipi icon is AI-generated original artwork, initially created with Grok
(xAI) and subsequently edited with Qwen-Image. It contains no upstream iTerm2
artwork. This provenance statement does not add an artwork license.
